  "docs.search.empty": "Nothing on any page matches that.",
  // STATES THE LIMIT RATHER THAN IMPLYING ITS ABSENCE. This search matches page
  // titles and summaries, not prose. An earlier draft read "Type to search every
  // page", which does not lie about any fact and still creates a belief the
  // product does not honour: it is the sentence a full-text search would write,
  // so a reader typing a phrase they remember from a paragraph gets nothing and
  // concludes the search is broken. Naming what is searched leaves no inference
  // to get wrong, and it stays true if prose is indexed later.
