  "console.memory.import.prompt.title": "Prompt to paste",
  "console.memory.import.prompt.hint": "Paste this into the source tool, then bring the report back here.",
  "console.memory.import.prompt.copy": "Copy prompt",
  "console.memory.import.prompt.copied": "Copied",
  "console.memory.import.prompt.copyFailed": "Copying was blocked. Select the prompt and copy it yourself.",
  "console.memory.import.prompt.all": 'Export everything you know about me and my work, from your saved memory and our past conversations, so I can bring it into Orvay. Preserve my words verbatim where possible, especially for instructions and preferences. Leave out passwords, keys, payment details, health details and other sensitive personal information, one-off tasks, and anything you are not sure is true. Do not invent anything.\n\n## Categories (output in this order):\n\n1. **Instructions**: Rules I have explicitly asked you to follow going forward: tone, format, style, "always do X", "never do Y", and corrections to your behavior.\n\n2. **Identity**: My name, where I am based, the languages I use, and the background that matters for my work.\n\n3. **Work**: My current and past roles, the company I work at, and my skill areas.\n\n4. **Company**: What my company does: its products, customers and market, the people and their roles, and important decisions and why they were made.\n\n5. **Projects**: Projects I meaningfully built or committed to. Ideally one entry per project, starting with its name, then what it does, its current status and any key decisions.\n\n6. **Preferences**: Opinions, tastes and working-style preferences that apply broadly.\n\n## Format:\n\nUse a heading for each category, written as ## and its name in English exactly as above, even if you write the entries in another language. Leave out a category you have nothing for. Within each category, list one entry per line, sorted by oldest date first, each entry one complete sentence of at most 300 characters. Format each line as:\n\n[YYYY-MM-DD] - Entry content here.\n\nIf no date is known, use [unknown] instead.\n\n## Output:\n- Wrap the entire export in a single code block for easy copying.\n- After the code block, state whether this is the complete set or if more remain.',
