  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // The site builder.
  //
  // A two-pane workbench: a brief on the left, the customer's site on the right.
  // The geometry is measured rather than designed and the reasoning for it is in
  // docs/research/lovable-measurements.md; what matters here is that two of these
  // sentences are DISCLOSURES rather than labels, and they are the reason the
  // screen is allowed to ship at all.
  //
  //   - `studio.offline.*` says the build service cannot be reached from this
  //     screen yet. It is not a loading state and it is not an error: it is the
  //     honest description of a surface whose backing service is not wired, which
  //     CLAUDE.md §12b requires in the words a customer would use rather than as
  //     a control that looks like it works.
  //   - `studio.blocking` says an answer arrives whole rather than a word at a
  //     time. There is no streaming anywhere in this product, so a caret typing
  //     itself across the pane would be an animation with no data behind it. The
  //     sentence exists so the wait is explained rather than faked.
  //
  // A translator should treat both as promises about behaviour and keep them
  // exactly as blunt as the English. Softening "nothing has been generated and
  // nothing has been spent" into a vaguer reassurance is the expensive direction:
  // the customer is being told what did NOT happen, and that is the half of the
  // sentence they need.
