  "studio.transcript.empty": "Nothing has run yet.",
  // RESTORED, NEVER REPLAYED, and this line is the whole of that distinction.
  //
  // The turns above it are the customer's own sentences, read back out of
  // storage when the page loaded. A thread that simply reappears above a caret
  // reads as an exchange that has just happened, which is the §12b failure in
  // its most forgivable costume: nothing is faked, and the screen still says
  // something untrue about when it happened.
  //
  // A translator must keep it in the PAST. "Continues from earlier" is a fact
  // about time, and a rendering that only says "your conversation" loses the one
  // thing the sentence is here to carry.
  "studio.history.show": "Show earlier conversation",
  "studio.history.hide": "Hide earlier conversation",
  "studio.transcript.restored": "This conversation continues from an earlier session.",
  // Asked, and no answer came back. Distinct from `studio.offline.*`, which is a
  // deployment with no build service attached at all: this one is wired, was
  // asked, and did not reply, so the screen genuinely does not know what exists.
  //
  // IT SAYS NOTHING IS LOST BECAUSE NOTHING IS. A site is stored away from this
  // screen and away from the container that previews it, so a failed read costs
  // the view of the work and never the work. That is the half a customer needs,
  // and a translator must keep it as blunt as the English.
  "studio.restore.unavailable": "Earlier builds did not load. Nothing is lost.",
