  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // THE CHROME'S FOUR SECTIONS, AND THE PAGES UNDER THEM (2026-09-05)
  //
  // The bar carried four triggers and reached eleven pages. The site has thirty
  // now, so the bar gained a section per group and the footer gained two
  // columns. Every label here is read by BOTH, from the same array in
  // `chrome.ts`, so the nav and the footer cannot disagree about what exists.
  //
  // A `.nav.blurb` is the one line a mega-nav entry shows under its title. It is
  // a separate key from the page's own `.lead` on purpose: a lead is written for
  // somebody already on the page and runs two sentences, and a panel entry has
  // room for about nine words.
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
