  "notification.headline.incident.opened": "Something went wrong with the company's work",
  "notification.headline.incident.critical": "Something went wrong that may reach people outside the company",
  "notification.summary.incident.critical": "An incident needs a person: open it to pause the work, take it over or stop it.",
  // ADR-0171 amended, 2026-11-01: published work that was confirmed is gone or changed. Mailed, never pushed. English only, in TRANSLATION_DEFERRED.
  "notification.headline.incident.regressed": "A published post or page that was confirmed is no longer there, or no longer says what it did",
  "notification.summary.incident.regressed": "A post or page the company published was confirmed when it went out, and a later check found it gone or changed. If somebody at the company removed or changed it on purpose, open the incident and choose Stop for good to close it.",
  // ADR-0150, 2026-10-22: unattended work waits once a channel has sent its hour's or day's share; what goes out by itself and what waits in Approvals. Translated.
  "notification.headline.crossing.rate_limited": "Some work has not gone out: one of your channels reached its limit for the hour or the day. Approved work, scheduled posts and workflows go out by themselves once there is room; open Approvals to send the rest.",
